 the will says and the estate handler are checked before anyone judges a price; any discount says who gives up value; no one signs until all three sisters confirm the process; the shared record stays open to correction; all three agree together on an independent valuer; and the valuation and proposed terms go to all three before anyone decides.

I disagree with the original draft as written: you and your husband buy now at a "family discount". It fails C's fair-share NCE, your valuation and clear-terms NCE, B's inclusion NCE, and our checked-facts NCE. I do not reject your hope to buy. I cannot judge it until the facts are known. The process draft fits the whole list: pause signatures, check the will and estate handler, agree together on an independent valuer, share the valuation and proposed terms with all three, then compare options with all three sisters heard. It leaves your purchase hope open. It does not yet set C's share or B's studio money, so it is not a final sale plan.

